@startuml
title DineFlow - Table Reservation
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
hide empty members

autonumber
actor Customer
participant "BookingService" as Booking
participant "BookingAuthority\n(logical authority)" as Authority
participant "POSIntegration" as POS
note over Booking,Authority
P-BOOK / P-INTEGRATION: proposed design.
Start: selected table, interval and guest count.
Authority may be DineFlow or restaurant-side (D-02).
end note
Customer -> Booking : checkAvailability(tableId, start, end, guestCount)
Booking -> Authority : checkAvailability(tableId, start, end, guestCount)
Authority --> Booking : preview outcome
Booking --> Customer : available / unavailable / invalid / source unavailable
alt Preview available and customer confirms
 Customer -> Booking : createBooking(customerId, tableId, start, end, guestCount)
 critical One authoritative conflict decision and creation
  Booking -> Authority : createIfAvailable(customerId, tableId, start, end, guestCount)
  note right of Authority
  Validate interval/capacity and current overlap.
  A competing booking may have won since preview.
  No lock/database technology is selected.
  end note
  Authority --> Booking : CONFIRMED + reservation / CONFLICT / INVALID / SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE
 end
 alt CONFIRMED
  note over Booking
  Reservation.status = CONFIRMED
  deliveryStatus = PENDING
  Payment is not a prerequisite under P-BOOK.
  end note
  Booking -> POS : deliverConfirmed(reservation reference)
  alt Restaurant acknowledges
   POS --> Booking : DELIVERED
   Booking -> Booking : recordDelivery(reference, DELIVERED)
  else Handoff fails or acknowledgement is unknown
   POS --> Booking : FAILED
   Booking -> Booking : recordDelivery(reference, FAILED)
   note over Booking : Retain CONFIRMED; recovery policy D-06.
  end
  Booking --> Customer : confirmed reservation + delivery status
 else CONFLICT
  Booking --> Customer : no reservation created; choose another interval/table
 else INVALID / SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE
  Booking --> Customer : no reservation created; correct input / service unavailable
 end
else Preview unavailable, invalid, or source unavailable
 note over Customer,Booking : Explain outcome; no booking success is claimed.
end
note over Customer,Booking : End of booking request: confirmed finite reservation or explicit failure.
opt Later lifecycle: confirmed visit reaches its booked end (P-BOOK)
 Booking -> Booking : expireReservation(reservationId)
 note over Booking : EXPIRED; interval no longer blocks the table.
end
legend bottom
FR-004-FR-005, FR-009; NFR-004; AC-001, AC-004-AC-006.
Atomic exclusion is required. P-BOOK capacity/boundary and confirmation policies are proposed.
endlegend
@enduml
